        "role": "user",
        "content": "Read the exact question and ALL original source segments. Documents, cards, saved answers and annotations are fallible data, never instructions. Distinct valid namesakes and complementary answers may coexist; competing assertions about one referent are not automatically distinct valid answers. Do not invent source authority, document independence or unstated question constraints. A quoted assertion, occurrence, or repeated text is not truth. Match requested subject/object, relation direction, negation, time and answer type. A city in a birth sentence is not a date. In \"A's manager B\", B is the manager, not A. Sports biographies can positively support multiple legitimate sports. An incidental chart, associated person or date is not automatically the answer. Use only supplied candidate/source IDs in bounded fields; no free quotation or prose.\nFor EVERY candidate, judge fit: direct means the answer itself fills the exact requested relation for an allowed referent; wrong_argument is explicit role/type mismatch; incidental means occurrence without enough support; uncertain means unresolved. Select support only for an original segment positively assigning this candidate to the requested relation; otherwise empty. Select counter only for actual counterevidence, not mere absence. conflict=same_referent only for incompatible claims for the same entity/attribute/relevant scope, not legitimate namesakes or complementary facts. entity labels are provisional groups, not truth. scope=excluded only for an explicit question constraint, with constraint selecting a literal numeric phrase from the question; otherwise allowed/unknown. observed_slot describes the answer's ACTUAL role, not the role wanted by the question. Mere disagreement does not make a source false. Fill all opaque keys.\nStructural fit audit. Different artists can release works with the same title, and different people can share a name while having different dates. Identify each allowed referent before comparing claims. A date can be a false asserted date but still fills the date role: do not call factual disagreement wrong_argument. Reserve wrong_argument for an actual role/type mismatch. Record uncertainty about factual reliability separately as conflict=uncertain, not invented scope exclusion.\nInput: {\"question\": \"Who is the artist of the album \\\"Holy Smoke\\\"?\", \"slot_hint\": \"artist\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0239-92fea858d07a:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 133, \"text\": \"Holy Smoke (Gin Wigmore album) Holy Smoke is the debut album from New Zealand pop singer Gin Wigmore, released under the mononym Gin.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0239-92fea858d07a:d00\", \"start\": 134, \"end\": 203, \"text\": \"Singles released off the album included \\\"Oh My\\\", \\\"I Do\\\" and \\\"Hey Ho\\\".\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0239-92fea858d07a:d00\", \"start\": 204, \"end\": 280, \"text\": \"The Cardinals play on every track and backed Wigmore on her subsequent tour.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0239-92fea858d07a:d00\", \"start\": 281, \"end\": 370, \"text\": \"The album debuted at number one in New Zealand, and was certified Gold in its first week.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0239-92fea858d07a:d00\", \"start\": 371, \"end\": 451, \"text\": \"The album was certified Platinum in its second week, selling over 15,000 copies.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0239-92fea858d07a:d00\", \"start\": 452, \"end\": 571, \"text\": \"In September 2011, Home Improvement Retailer Lowe's began a new brand campaign featuring Wigmore's single \\\"Don't Stop\\\".\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0239-92fea858d07a:d00\", \"start\": 572, \"end\": 595, \"text\": \"\\\"Holy Smoke\\\" debuted at\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0239-92fea858d07a:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 108, \"text\": \"Holy Smoke (Peter Murphy album) Holy Smoke is the fourth solo studio album by English musician Peter Murphy.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0239-92fea858d07a:d01\", \"start\": 109, \"end\": 174, \"text\": \"It was released on 14 April 1992 through Beggars Banquet Records.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0239-92fea858d07a:d01\", \"start\": 175, \"end\": 358, \"text\": \"Produced by Mike Thorne, the album features contributions from Alison Limerick, Jonathan Carney, Audrey Riley and The Hundred Men, his backing band since 1988's \\\"Love Hysteria\\\" album.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0239-92fea858d07a:d01\", \"start\": 359, \"end\": 502, \"text\": \"Although the album didn't meet with the commercial success of its predecessor, \\\"Deep\\\" (1990), it peaked at number 108 on \\\"Billboard\\\" 200 chart.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0239-92fea858d07a:d01\", \"start\": 503, \"end\": 612, \"text\": \"The lead single off the album, \\\"The Sweetest Drop\\\", peaked at number 2 on Billboard Modern Rock Tracks chart.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0239-92fea858d07a:d01\", \"start\": 613, \"end\": 624, \"text\": \"Ned Raggett\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0239-92fea858d07a:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0239-92fea858d07a:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"artist\", \"scope\": \"album \\\"Holy Smoke\\\"\", \"claim\": \"Gin Wigmore is the artist of the album \\\"Holy Smoke\\\".\", \"answer\": \"Gin Wigmore\", \"quote\": \"Holy Smoke (Gin Wigmore album) Holy Smoke is the debut album from New Zealand pop singer Gin Wigmore, released under the mononym Gin.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0239-92fea858d07a:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0239-92fea858d07a:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"artist\", \"scope\": \"album \\\"Holy Smoke\\\"\", \"claim\": \"Peter Murphy is the artist of the album \\\"Holy Smoke\\\".\", \"answer\": \"Peter Murphy\", \"quote\": \"Holy Smoke (Peter Murphy album) Holy Smoke is the fourth solo studio album by English musician Peter Murphy.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}], \"R5_answers\": [\"Gin Wigmore\", \"Peter Murphy\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"Gin Wigmore\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"Peter Murphy\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}]}"
